      "writtenOn": "2021-11-09T13:43:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For the short term, I put in a bool type as you suggested. I also made a change to LoopFloat/LoopInt to make the outcome not-entirely-deterministic (it now depends on a uniform) so that we could actually get to see how this stuff looks when there\u0027s real code. It\u0027s still only uniforms, though, so it\u0027s all hoisted.\n\nI think a map of slots to full names is a good starting point. We\u0027ll want it in the trace and in the skslc output. We do run the risk of getting chatty results like\n\nresultColor.r:  0.0\nresultColor.g:  1.0\nresultColor.b:  0.0\nresultColor.a:  1.0\n\nWhen we want\n\nresultColor: (0.0, 1.0, 0.0, 1.0)\n\nbut we can cross that bridge when we get to it.",
      "parentUuid": "b26858dd_2cb512f1",
